    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The path",
      "items": [
        "Preflight, bump, commit X, suite, evidence commit X+1, seal, tag",
        "X carries the code and the bump; X+1 carries evidence only",
        "The tag is created only on X+1, right after the push"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The refusals",
      "items": [
        "Each step guards invariants I1..I8 and refuses, never warns",
        "A refusal names the invariant and exits non-zero",
        "A red tag is a wait: nothing reaches npm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why two commits",
      "items": [
        "The suite measures X, then the evidence is recorded after it",
        "Never amend X after the record: it would orphan the snapshot",
        "The human writes the changelog; the script enforces the order"
      ]
    }
